From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 13:58:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] third_party: vendor Stylo with the eager pseudo-element
 cascade skip

Build the Stylo crates from third_party/stylo through a `[patch]` table
instead of the crates.io packages that Servo's releases take. The `stylo`
dependency keeps upstream's version requirement exactly as upstream Servo
writes it, and third_party/patches/stylo/update.sh reads it: it fetches
servo/stylo at the release tag of that version (or at the commit of a
git pin, as on upstream's main branch), applies the patches next to it and copies the tracked files (minus upstream's CI and
git configuration) into third_party/stylo, so an upstream bump of the pin
only needs a re-run of the script. `update.sh --export-patches`
regenerates the patches from a Stylo checkout and `update.sh --check`
verifies the committed copy. Cargo applies the table only if the
vendored crates have the versions the dependencies require, which
vendoring the release tag ensures. The whole of third_party is now excluded
from the workspace; the nested Stylo workspace manifest is needed for its
crates' `workspace = true` fields.

The one patch, also proposed upstream, skips cascading the style of a
::before/::after whose matched rules declare no `content`. Such a
pseudo-element cannot generate a box, so Stylo threw the cascaded style
away; universal rules like Tailwind's `*, ::before, ::after { --tw-...: ... }`
made that half of all style traversal work on the GenUI pages. On a
HarmonyOS phone with `--pref=layout_threads=1` (two A/B rounds, 20 loads each)
`layout_proper` drops by 16% (chuxing), 17% (biyadi), 26% (shibashiji)
and 16% (keai), and `traverse_dom` by 41-47%; the default three layout
threads confirm it. Rendering is unchanged: the same pseudo-elements were
already discarded after the cascade.

Validation: `third_party/patches/stylo/update.sh --check` reproduces the committed copy. `./mach check --ohos`, `./mach fmt` and `./mach test-tidy` pass. With the same Stylo patch as a path dependency, `./mach test-wpt --release css/css-pseudo css/css-content css/cssom css/css-transitions css/css-animations css/css-nesting css/css-lists css/selectors css/css-cascade css/css-variables` runs with no unexpected results. 2026-11-09 sync: `update.sh --check` reproduces the copy vendored from Stylo v0.23.0, whose crates.io package names that tag's commit (2dca34592ce) in .cargo_vcs_info.json, and which is the git pin 890aa121c6 of the release's branch point with the crate versions bumped; `cargo metadata --locked` passes, and Cargo.lock takes all 11 Stylo crates from third_party/stylo, with no unused patch.
